cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "FLASH: A Generate Once, Synthesize Many Framework for Synthetic Anomaly Generation in Industrial Anomaly Detection"
abstract: >-
  FLASH decouples defect generation from anomaly synthesis. A small set of defect instances is
  generated once from defect-free images, validated, and banked; those defects are then reused to
  compose a much larger anomaly corpus without invoking a generator again. Defect masks are
  recovered from the generated images rather than prescribed in advance, so labels cannot drift
  from the images they describe.
message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite the paper."
